## Production security defaults

These scaffold defaults are safe for local development and must change
before production. Details: `docs/explanations/security-defaults.md`
(if the render ships no docs tree, read the same page in the template
repository).

- Never commit real secrets: `.env`, `.envs/`, `*.pem` stay git-ignored
  (`.gitignore`), and `.env.example` carries only placeholder/commented
  values. The hygiene CI rejects committed secrets.

{% if mcp_effective %}
- The MCP server defaults to stdio (localhost-only). Binding
  `--host 0.0.0.0` (e.g. inside Docker) requires `MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS`
  (`mcp_server.py` refuses to start without it): set it to the exact host
  allowlist, plus `MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` for the browsers that may call it.
  `GET /health` on the MCP server is unauthenticated (orchestrator probe).
{% endif %}
{% if bot_discord_effective %}
- `DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN` is required (`bot_discord.py` refuses to start
  without it): inject it from the environment, never bake it into the
  image or commit it.
{% endif %}
{% if bot_slack_effective %}
- `SLACK_BOT_TOKEN` (xoxb-) and `SLACK_APP_TOKEN` (xapp-,
  `connections:write`) are both required (`bot_slack.py` refuses to start
  without either): inject them from the environment, never bake them into
  the image or commit them.
{% endif %}
{% if bot_line_effective %}
- `LINE_CHANNEL_SECRET` and `LINE_CHANNEL_ACCESS_TOKEN` are both required
  (`bot_line.py` refuses to start without either): the secret verifies
  `X-Line-Signature` on every `POST /callback`, which is what makes the
  public webhook safe. The webhook listens on all interfaces (`BOT_PORT`,
  default 8000): expose it over HTTPS only (signature + TLS).
{% endif %}
{% if bot_gmail_effective %}
- `GMAIL_CREDENTIALS_JSON` / `GMAIL_TOKEN_JSON` are required file paths
  (`bot_gmail.py` refuses to start without either): mount them read-only
  (e.g. `/run/secrets/`) — the token file IS the inbox. Both stay
  git-ignored (`/credentials.json`, `/token.json`).
{% endif %}
{% if include_sentry %}
- `SENTRY_DSN` ships unset and `sentry_sdk.init` samples all traces
  (`traces_sample_rate=1.0`): set the DSN from the environment in
  production and lower the sample rate (scrub PII before enabling it).
{% endif %}
{% if scraping_effective %}
- `FETCHER_CONTACT` ships as the `contact@example.com` placeholder (the
  fetcher User-Agent carries it): set a reachable address before any real
  crawl, and keep the 1 req/s-per-host politeness floor (`CHARTER.md`).
{% endif %}


{% if ctf_effective %}
- CTF targets and flags stay out of git (`challenges/**/vuln`,
  `challenges/**/flag*` are git-ignored): never commit binaries or flags.
{% endif %}

## Commits and CI

- Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)
  (`feat:`, `fix:`, ...) in the PR title — hygiene CI checks the title
  only, and pull requests land via squash-merge. Individual commit messages
  are free-form.
- CI runs lint, type-check, and tests on every push
{% if docs %} plus a docs build{% endif %}; keep all of them green.
